# Story: As a truck driver, I want to move my booking to another slot, so that I can keep my container booked when I am running late. Rescheduling moves the booking to the new slot if it has room, frees the place in the old slot, and keeps the same booking reference. Moving to a full slot is refused with SLOT_FULL; moving to the same slot is refused with SAME_SLOT.

@draft
Feature: Rescheduling a Booking

  Scenario Outline: A driver reschedules their booking to another slot with room
    Given I am a driver
    And I book that slot for container "<container>"
    When the slot has <room> place left
    Then the outcome is "RESCHEDULED"
    Examples:
      | container | room        |
      | ABC123    | 1          |
      | DEF456    | 2          |

  Scenario Outline: A driver tries to reschedule their booking to a full slot
    Given I am a driver
    And I book that slot for container "<container>"
    When the slot has 0 place left
    Then the outcome is "SLOT_FULL"
    Examples:
      | container |
      | ABC123    |

  Scenario Outline: A driver tries to reschedule their booking to the same slot
    Given I am a driver
    And I book that slot for container "<container>"
    When another driver books that slot
    Then the outcome is "SAME_SLOT"
    Examples:
      | container |
      | ABC123    |

  Scenario: A driver tries to reschedule their booking after check-in
    Given I am a driver
    And I book that slot for container "<container>"
    When another driver books that slot
    And a clerk checks the truck in
    Then the change is refused because "CHANGE_CUTOFF_PASSED"
